## script that wrote this log
    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 5 part 6 P3 run.log (specs/0037-measurement-and-close.md, "P3:
    # the close", "Harness runs" and "The engineering close"; decisions 1 to 3
    # all A; planning's rulings A to V, and W during P3, held uncommitted in the
    # working spec):
    #   1. the release binaries: the size log's, copied and checked against the
    #      hashes size.log printed, both targets (this log builds none);
    #   2. the seven samples of ruling W over the corpus, each on both targets,
    #      with the size log's binaries: part 5 P4's chartlabels, removechart,
    #      chartmore, chart3d and charts, and part 4 P3's addchart and
    #      chartkinds (<runs>/<utc-date>-<shortsha>-<sample>); every row ok,
    #      every input and output opening in LibreOffice, no leftover, the two
    #      labels' outputs and lines the same; and every run's rows, output and
    #      line, byte-identical by sha256 to the earlier run of its sample, the
    #      one its committed record names (part 5 P4's for the first five, part
    #      4 P3's for addchart and chartkinds), --charts-sample's run against
    #      both of its records' runs, part 5 P4's and part 4 P3's, 27 of 27 on
    #      each label, each earlier run's summaries its record's summary table
    #      (part 4 ruling S's reading; a difference is a finding);
    #   3. each run's record pair, m5p6-p3-<sample>-<utc-date>-<shortsha>, .md
    #      and .txt, checked against its run directory table by table (M5 part 6
    #      P2's corrected record check, rulings Q and R);
    #   4. the CHANGELOG's citation check and form: a "Fixed" section added
    #      after "Changed" with one bullet citing specs/0037 (decision 3 A);
    #   5. the host keep regenerated, compared with the last committed
    #      open-check record, M5 part 6 P2's, named by its record commit: the
    #      phase's two new tests keep one new pair each, none changed or gone,
    #      and opened by scripts/edit-open-check.sh, recorded as
    #      m5p6-open-<utc-date>-<shortsha>;
    #   6. this script's own standard error counted (specs/0017 P1 verification
    #      ruling 7).
    # No text, title, series name, formula, sheet name, part name, target or
    # path from the corpus is printed: workbook ids, counts, flags and hashes
    # only.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M5 part 6 P3 from M5 part 5 P4's run script (printed in
    # records/logs/m5p5-p4/run.log; its header and change lists, NVZ to NWF
    # and the history before them, follow), generated by
    # <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p6-p3/gen/run.py from that text and P4's code,
    # each replacement asserted to occur once; the record check program is M5
    # part 6 P2's regenerated run script's (specs/0037 ruling R). The CHANGELOG
    # check's two programs, M4 part 2 P1's changelog_check.py and p1_checks.sh,
    # are copied beside this script, as part 5 P4's were. The labels go on from
    # P4's NWF. What differs, and why:
    #  NWG. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p6-p3/scripts, on the disk),
    #      the keep (<home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p6-p3/keep-host) and the
    #      target root (<home>/.cache/emend-build/m5p6-p3/target) are this
    #      phase's; the spec is specs/0037, pinned at the committed blob the
    #      doc commit c4b2598 holds (SPEC_WANT), and planning's rulings during
